<%# locals: (person:, src:) %>
<%#
  One person's history, fetched only once their row is first opened. The frame
  id is the contract with detail.html.erb, which renders the reply into it.

  target: "_top" so the note links inside the frame navigate the whole page.
  Without it Turbo would try to resolve the person-layout note form into this
  frame, find no matching id, and raise turbo:frame-missing. The frame's own
  lazy src still renders here -- target only governs navigations started from
  inside the frame.

  The /mentoring/convert-prospectives table wraps this in a row carrying
  uf_detail_id(person) and the hidden/aria-hidden state the toggle controller
  drives.
%>
<%= turbo_frame_tag "uf-frame-#{person.id}", target: "_top", src: src, loading: "lazy" do %>
  <p class="text-body my-2">Loading <%= person.callsign %>&rsquo;s history&hellip;</p>
<% end %>
